<folder_context path="adapters/submodule">

<reusable_module_context name="Git submodule adapter">
This ordinary adapter owns one Git submodule binding. The lifecycle passes the durable binding
path in Export.Path; an empty path defaults to deps/DEPENDENCY_ALIAS. Pull materialises or
recreates the exact resolved LockedDependency.Commit, Remove deletes only the matching clean
submodule, and Inspect reads index and checkout state without mutation.
</reusable_module_context>

<system_invariant name="Exact detached commit">
The parent index entry is mode 160000 at the locked commit and the submodule checkout is detached
at that same commit. Updates use fetch plus checkout --detach. Never run git pull and never use a
force option.
</system_invariant>

<critical_system_mandates name="Protect user Git state">
Reject unsafe or symlinked paths, unmerged index entries, non-gitlink collisions, source identity
mismatches, dirty submodules, and removal of a checkout not registered to this binding. A failed
new add restores the original .gitmodules bytes and removes only Git/worktree residue created by
that attempt. Existing clean materialisations roll back their checkout and index entry when an
update fails after checkout.
</critical_system_mandates>

<system_invariant name="Narrow local protocol opt-in">
Only Git commands that access a file:// source receive -c protocol.file.allow=always. Repository
or global Git configuration is never weakened.
</system_invariant>

<verification_and_unit_test_criteria>
Local bare-repository fixtures cover exact add and pull commits, detached HEAD, gitlink and
.gitmodules registration, idempotence, dirty pull/removal refusal, collision refusal, complete
safe removal, and file-protocol scoping.
</verification_and_unit_test_criteria>

</folder_context>
